--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The container images
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The control plane's and the agent's images are built on Eclipse Temurin's JRE
on Alpine Linux (`eclipse-temurin:25-jre-alpine`); the demonstration report
plugin's on Google's distroless Java image (`gcr.io/distroless/java25-debian13`).
Both pinned by digest in the build. Those base layers are separate programs
aggregated beside Vectispire's jar, not linked into it:

  the JRE                    GPL-2.0 with the Classpath Exception (OpenJDK)
  busybox, apk-tools, coreutils, alpine-baselayout, scanelf, ssl_client, netbase,
  base-files                 GPL-2.0 or GPL-3.0
  musl, glibc, libattr, acl-libs, libintl, libtasn1, libcrypt
                             MIT, LGPL-2.1 or later
  the GCC runtime            GPL-3.0 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception
  OpenSSL, zlib, libpng, FreeType, fontconfig, the DejaVu fonts, the CA bundle
                             Apache-2.0, Zlib, Libpng, FTL, MIT-style,
                             Bitstream Vera, MPL-2.0

Each package's own license is in the image (`/usr/share/doc`, `/lib/apk/db`)
and is checked against `ci/licences/allowed.txt` from the images' SBOMs.
The source of every GPL and LGPL package in them is the distribution's, at
the version the image carries: https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports,
https://sources.debian.org, and https://github.com/adoptium/jdk25u for the JRE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scanners invoked as containers
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Vectispire runs each scanner as an ephemeral container, by command line, in a
separate process. It bundles none of them and links against none of them; the
images are pulled at run time from their own publishers.

  Syft, Grype           Anchore                   Apache-2.0
  checkov               Prisma Cloud/Bridgecrew   Apache-2.0
  gitleaks              Zachary Rice              MIT
  Semgrep OSS           Semgrep, Inc.             LGPL-2.1

The Semgrep *rules* are a separate question from the Semgrep engine, and the
one place where a licence decides how the code is shaped. Vectispire bundles a
single rule of its own and redistributes no third-party rule set. An operator
who wants real coverage has Vectispire fetch `opengrep/opengrep-rules` — LGPL-2.1
with a Commons Clause, accepted explicitly because that clause takes whoever
adopts those rules out of open source in the OSI sense. The rules travel from
their author to that installation; nothing containing them is shipped here.
`semgrep/semgrep-rules` is refused outright, by constant rather than by
convention, because its terms forbid distribution at all. See
`RuleCatalogue` and decision 0006.

Vulnerability and lifecycle data reached over the network — the EPSS scores
(FIRST.org), the CISA KEV catalog and endoflife.date — is neither bundled nor
redistributed, and carries its publishers' own terms of use.
